---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: steward-node-src-seam-birth-rule
purpose: >
  steward/node (`elohim-node`) — the household hub-cluster runtime: pod
  consensus-gathering (`src/pod/consensus.rs`: ConsensusManager::request_consensus/
  ConsensusOutcome) and admission-control backpressure (`src/pod/admission.rs`:
  AdmissionController::evaluate/AdmissionDecision/DeferReason), plus the axum
  dashboard (`src/dashboard/`). `steward/node/seam-registry.yaml` already
  registers this crate's decision surface. This manifest adds ONE edit-time
  signal (plan task P4.5, the seam-concern contract architecture's design-time
  birth rule): catch the NEXT decision surface before it ships unregistered.
rules:
  - id: seam-birth-rule
    class: inject
    when:
      write: "*.rs"
      contains-any: ["Decision {", "Verdict {", "Outcome {", "Reason {",
                     "Disposition {", "fn decide_", "Answer<", ".route(",
                     "match (method"]
    dedupe-of: ".claude/skills/p2p-design-gate/SKILL.md (Step 4: Concern-Canon Answer) + steward/node/seam-registry.yaml (this crate's decision-point registry) — where a new decision surface answers the canon and gets registered"
    why: >
      This shape (a verdict/decision/outcome/reason enum, a `decide_*` predicate,
      an `Answer<T>` boundary type, or a route registration) is exactly what the
      seam-concern contract architecture's birth rule governs: a NEW decision
      predicate, boundary answer type, sync message, or route may not be born
      unregistered. Before shipping one: walk `p2p-design-gate` Step 4 — answer
      C0-C14 (`answered`/`partial`/`unbound`/`n-a`-with-justification) against the
      guarantee in its canon home (predicate-bearing classes are enforcement rows
      in `.claude/epr-meta/policies.yaml`, currently C2/C6a; the rest are
      Precedent-shaped rows in `.claude/epr-meta/concerns.yaml`) — then add a row
      to `steward/node/seam-registry.yaml` (schema:
      `elohim/sdk/schemas/v1/manifest/seam-registry.schema.json`). The census
      (`placement-audit.py --epr-meta`) is the enforcement backstop, not this
      advisory: it fails loud on an unregistered point, an uncited contract test,
      or a mirrored test. This is the exact seam the plan's own seeded forecast
      names as unbound-and-unregistered today (C1 at
      ConsensusManager::request_consensus — self-election is the definitional
      question here and nothing currently excludes the proposer from its own
      approver set). This rule matches file CONTENT, not added lines, so an edit
      anywhere in an already-registered file (`pod/consensus.rs`,
      `pod/admission.rs`) re-fires too — the accepted cost of a declarative
      advisory that never blocks (never a validator: this is a judgement call,
      not a textual proof).
cites:
  - seam-concern-contract-architecture-plan
---

# steward/node/src — seam birth rule (concern canon)

`../CLAUDE.md`/`../ARCHITECTURE.md` and this crate's `seam-registry.yaml` describe
the decision surface itself; this manifest only adds the edit-time reminder that a
*new* one (plan task P4.5) must answer the concern canon and register before it
ships. See `.claude/epr-meta/policies.yaml` + `.claude/epr-meta/concerns.yaml` for
the sixteen classes (C0-C14, C6 split C6a/C6b) and the `p2p-design-gate` skill's
Step 4 for the per-class checklist.
